WEBVTT

NOTE Unofficial English translation of the Thai narration. If it differs from the Thai original documents, the Thai original prevails.

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:05.680
The Senate Committee on
Agriculture and Cooperatives

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:10.260
held Meeting No. 36/2569 on
Monday, 26 October 2026.

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:14.855
Mr. Sountorn Chaokijka, the committee
chair, presided over the meeting.

00:00:14.935 --> 00:00:19.636
First, the meeting noted
three Cabinet resolutions of

00:00:19.636 --> 00:00:24.159
20 October concerning
agriculture and cooperatives.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:29.372
One: measures to assist,
compensate and restore

00:00:29.372 --> 00:00:32.419
those affected by the 2026 floods.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:35.752
Including credit from
the Bank for Agriculture

00:00:35.752 --> 00:00:38.863
and Agricultural
Cooperatives, for liquidity

00:00:38.863 --> 00:00:41.479
and to repair damaged farm equipment.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:46.862
Two: measures to stabilise paddy prices
under the concept "Thai Rice for the

00:00:46.862 --> 00:00:52.164
Future Economy": five projects within
a budget frame of 58,000 million baht.

00:00:52.245 --> 00:00:57.675
Three: measures to stabilise
feed maize prices and

00:00:57.675 --> 00:01:02.779
promote production for
the 2026/2027 crop year.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:09.084
The meeting also noted that on 29
September the Cabinet acknowledged the

00:01:09.084 --> 00:01:14.315
results of considering the study
report on managing Thai farm household

00:01:14.315 --> 00:01:19.177
debt, as proposed by the Ministry
of Agriculture and Cooperatives.

00:01:19.259 --> 00:01:23.880
The meeting then considered progress
reports from its subcommittees.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:29.160
The committee's three current
subcommittees are chaired as follows.

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:32.820
Livestock and Fisheries:
Mr. Ruchu Kaewlai.

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:39.160
Water Management in Farm Areas Outside
Irrigation Zones: Miss Amorn Sribunnak.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:43.580
And Integrated Agricultural
Networks: Mr. Choocheep Auekarn.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:49.423
The Integrated Agricultural Networks
subcommittee reported progress

00:01:49.423 --> 00:01:54.193
on its draft report, analysing
structural problems along the whole

00:01:54.193 --> 00:01:58.819
chain, from research and production
to processing and marketing.

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:02.649
The study highlights eight key
problems, such as a lack of

00:02:02.649 --> 00:02:06.527
integration between agencies,
databases that are not linked,

00:02:06.527 --> 00:02:09.759
and farm goods being sold
mainly as raw materials.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:14.200
It proposes urgent, medium-term
and long-term measures.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:20.020
And proposes pilot projects tested in
real areas before scaling up nationwide.

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:24.257
The Water Management
subcommittee is revising

00:02:24.257 --> 00:02:26.558
the content of its draft report.

00:02:26.639 --> 00:02:31.335
Covering a comparison of five pilot
provinces, and reviewing groundwater

00:02:31.335 --> 00:02:35.379
banks as one option depending on
the suitability of each area.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:39.696
Its policy recommendations
stress provincial water data

00:02:39.696 --> 00:02:43.777
centres, data integration
between agencies, community

00:02:43.777 --> 00:02:47.858
participation, and prioritising
projects and budgets.

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:53.703
The Livestock and Fisheries subcommittee
is gathering and analysing data

00:02:53.703 --> 00:02:58.479
from government agencies, the private
sector and academic institutions.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:05.220
It plans a study visit to Uthai
Thani from 12 to 13 November.

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:11.522
To study the management of a stray dog
shelter, animal population control,

00:03:11.522 --> 00:03:16.399
sterilisation, rabies vaccination
and veterinary services.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:21.604
The meeting considered replies from the
Department of Livestock Development

00:03:21.604 --> 00:03:25.639
and the Ministry of Commerce on
exporting halal beef to the Middle East.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:30.716
The agencies explained the food safety
requirements, halal certification and

00:03:30.716 --> 00:03:35.318
registration of establishments for
export to the United Arab Emirates.

00:03:35.399 --> 00:03:39.050
The operator's company is already
halal-certified, so it can

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:42.519
file its registration request
through the relevant steps.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:46.600
The meeting agreed to inform the
complainant and close the matter.

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:52.405
The meeting also considered a draft
schedule for a study visit on water

00:03:52.405 --> 00:03:56.939
resource management for the development
of agriculture and farmers.

00:03:57.020 --> 00:04:02.620
In Trang, from Thursday
26 to Friday 27 November.

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:06.580
This summary is based on the
committee's press release.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:09.610
Meeting minutes and reports
are available through

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:12.379
the channels of the
Secretariat of the Senate.

